envadjust: rebase each frame off the new stack, not off the freed one.

stack_extend_alloc() hands the old VM stack to mrb_realloc() and then calls
envadjust(), which moved every frame's pointer with `ci->stack += delta`.
That is pointer arithmetic on a pointer realloc has already freed. On an
ordinary allocator it computes the right address and nothing happens; in a
Capstone domain whose free revokes, the result is derived from a revoked
capability, carries no tag, and the next write through it faults (cause 24).
It is what stopped `MRBD_HEAP=sublet` and `sublet-gc` at ~40 frames of Ruby
recursion, which is shallow enough that the port's own scripts/smoke.rb hit
it.

This is upstream's own defect and upstream's own fix: e5c82761f, "vm.c: fix
envadjust rebasing stack pointers off a freed pointer" (2026-07-24), found
when another memory-safe C implementation trapped on exactly this write. The
fix derives each frame from newbase instead, which yields the identical
address and carries the new buffer's bounds. That commit does not apply here
because it rewrites the byte-level form introduced by d95ebe4a2, which landed
after this pin; the expression it settles on is used verbatim.

Only 4.0.0-rc2 needs this. The port's `head` pin already carries d95ebe4a2 and
e5c82761f, so its envadjust is already rebased off newbase.

diff --git i/src/vm.c w/src/vm.c
index f898287d8..56d6bec42 100644
--- i/src/vm.c
+++ w/src/vm.c
@@ -134,19 +134,26 @@ static inline void
 envadjust(mrb_state *mrb, mrb_value *oldbase, mrb_value *newbase)
 {
   mrb_callinfo *ci = mrb->c->cibase;
-  ptrdiff_t delta = newbase - oldbase;
 
-  if (delta == 0) return;
+  if (newbase == oldbase) return;
+
   while (ci <= mrb->c->ci) {
     struct REnv *e = mrb_vm_ci_env(ci);
 
+    /* Derive each frame's new pointer from newbase, never from the old one:
+       stack_extend_alloc() has already handed the old stack to mrb_realloc(),
+       so `ci->stack + delta` is pointer arithmetic on a freed pointer. It
+       computes the right address on an ordinary allocator and traps on an
+       implementation that tracks provenance and bounds. */
+    mrb_value *new_stack = (mrb_value *)((char *)newbase + ((char *)ci->stack - (char *)oldbase));
+
     if (e) {
       mrb_assert(e->cxt == mrb->c && MRB_ENV_ONSTACK_P(e));
       mrb_assert(e->stack == ci->stack);
 
-      e->stack += delta;
+      e->stack = new_stack;
     }
-    ci->stack += delta;
+    ci->stack = new_stack;
     ci++;
   }
 }
